                <pb facs="0187" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/281: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-01T11:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 1,
                                1926—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 1—9:03
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. Your 81, March 31, 6 p.m. According to the <hi rendition="#italic">Journal
                        Officiel</hi> following is the statement of the Minister of Finance: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“As to interallied debts it goes without saying that we are not going to
                            discuss them at this moment. The negotiations with the United States,
                            with England, continue, in a spirit of friendliness on the part of these
                            two countries, with a very great desire for conciliation on the side of
                            France.</p>
                        <p>As for myself, [Gentlemen,] I shall do my utmost to have this thesis
                            prevail, that French payments should be fixed equitably in proportion to
                            those that she will receive from Germany.”<anchor n="2" xml:id="d55-f1"
                            /></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Mailed to London, Rome, Brussels, and Berlin. Copy to European Information
                    Center.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
